   "act": "Manim exhibit — Hubble recession velocity vs distance",
   "narration_text": "Each point is a galaxy. Its position on the x-axis is its distance in megaparsecs; its height is its recession velocity in kilometers per second. The cloud scatters, but the slope is unmistakable — a linear relationship from origin to the edge of the observable sample. The slope is H-zero. That slope is the expansion rate of the universe.",
